      {
        title: "6. Observability, Resilience and Disaster Recovery",
        explanation:
          "Production architecture must make service health visible and define how the system recovers from failure. CloudWatch metrics, alarms and logs help teams observe infrastructure and application behavior. CloudTrail provides an audit record of supported API activity, while VPC Flow Logs provide network traffic metadata. Resilience requires eliminating unnecessary single points of failure, setting meaningful health checks, testing failover and controlling dependencies. Disaster recovery adds a wider recovery strategy for regional or major infrastructure events. Backup and restore, pilot light, warm standby and multi-site active-active designs have different recovery times, operational complexity and costs. The correct approach depends on business impact rather than choosing the most expensive option by default.",
        responsibilities: [
          "CloudWatch: metrics, logs, dashboards and alarms.",
          "CloudTrail: AWS API audit history.",
          "VPC Flow Logs: network interface traffic metadata.",
          "AWS Backup: policy-driven backup management for supported resources.",
          "Route 53: DNS routing policies that can support recovery designs."
