        implementation: [
          "Provision a managed certificate or another supported TLS certificate arrangement.",
          "Create the forwarding rule, target HTTPS proxy, URL map and backend service.",
          "Configure health checks that verify application readiness rather than only process existence.",
          "Attach Cloud Armor policies based on application threat and traffic requirements.",
          "Enable Cloud CDN only for routes and response types with correct caching behavior.",
          "Publish DNS records after validating the load-balancer frontend and certificate."
        ],
        productionConsiderations: [
          "Separate liveness from readiness so unhealthy instances are not sent production traffic.",
          "Set realistic health-check thresholds and understand how quickly backends are removed.",
          "Do not cache personalized or sensitive responses without explicit cache-control design.",
          "Test certificate renewal, DNS changes and backend failover procedures.",
          "Review logs and security policy outcomes during traffic spikes and attack simulations."
        ],
        failureModes: [
