      {
        "question": "What problem does Public and Private Subnets solve?",
        "answer": "Public and private subnets divide a VPC into workload zones with different routing and exposure characteristics. Their design determines which resources can receive inbound internet traffic and which remain internal. It provides a defined way to organize the components and responsibilities involved. In a production environment, the design should be selected according to workload requirements, security boundaries, operational capability and measurable service objectives."
