    "interviewQuestions": [
      {
        "question": "What problem does Route Tables solve?",
        "answer": "Route tables determine where network traffic is forwarded. Each subnet uses an associated route table, and the most specific matching route controls the next hop for a destination. It provides a defined way to organize the components and responsibilities involved. In a production environment, the design should be selected according to workload requirements, security boundaries, operational capability and measurable service objectives."
      },
      {
        "question": "Which components should an engineer understand first?",
