        "question": "What problem does Application Load Balancer solve?",
        "answer": "An Application Load Balancer distributes HTTP and HTTPS requests across registered targets. Listener rules support host-based and path-based routing, TLS termination and health-based traffic distribution. It provides a defined way to organize the components and responsibilities involved. In a production environment, the design should be selected according to workload requirements, security boundaries, operational capability and measurable service objectives."
      },
