        ],
        "title": "Failure Analysis, Troubleshooting and Validation",
        "productionConsiderations": [
          "Maintain an incident runbook with commands and rollback criteria.",
          "Preserve evidence before making disruptive changes.",
          "Track recurring incidents and convert findings into automated safeguards."
        ],
        "explanation": "Important failure patterns include: Incorrect listener priority, unhealthy targets, certificate expiry, path-rule mismatch and health-check endpoint failures. Troubleshooting should start with the user-visible symptom and move through the architecture one boundary at a time. Check recent changes, component health, access decisions, routing, dependency status and telemetry. Validate the recovery with a real request or workload test, then document the root cause and preventive action.",
        "failureModes": [
          "Troubleshooting changes multiple variables and hides the original cause.",
          "A superficial health check passes while the real user path remains broken.",
          "The same failure returns because the root cause was not addressed."
        ],
