        "answer": "Amazon S3 stores objects in buckets and supports application assets, backups, data lakes and static content. Production design covers access policies, encryption, lifecycle, versioning, replication and recovery. It provides a defined way to organize the components and responsibilities involved. In a production environment, the design should be selected according to workload requirements, security boundaries, operational capability and measurable service objectives."
