        ],
        "explanation": "Kubernetes manages containerized workloads through API objects and reconciliation controllers. A reliable design considers control-plane availability, scheduling, service discovery, storage, security and rollout behavior. The design flow is kubectl or CI -> API Server -> Controllers and Scheduler -> Nodes and Pods -> Services and Ingress -> Persistent Storage. Treat each boundary as an explicit responsibility: identify who owns the component, which interface it exposes, what data or traffic crosses it, and how its health is measured. Keep the architecture aligned with workload requirements instead of adding services without a clear operational reason.",
        "failureModes": [
          "A hidden dependency fails and interrupts downstream components.",
          "An undocumented configuration change creates behavior different from the approved design.",
          "Capacity or dependency limits are reached before monitoring detects the problem."
        ],
