        "explanation": "The primary building blocks are API server, scheduler, controllers, etcd, deployments, services, ingress, config maps, secrets and persistent volumes. Follow a request or data item from its source through every component until it reaches its destination. At each hop, verify the protocol, identity, routing decision, transformation and response path. This end-to-end view helps engineers distinguish a component failure from a connectivity, authorization or application-level problem.",
        "failureModes": [
          "A missing interface or route breaks communication between components.",
          "A dependency returns errors while the primary component remains healthy.",
          "A configuration mismatch causes partial or intermittent traffic failure."
