        ],
        "title": "Security, Resilience and Operational Controls",
        "productionConsiderations": [
          "Review access and policy changes regularly.",
          "Test recovery and failover procedures with measurable objectives.",
          "Keep security evidence and operational runbooks available to responders."
        ],
        "explanation": "Production controls for this architecture include: Use namespaces, RBAC, resource requests and limits, probes, network policies, disruption budgets and tested upgrade procedures. Apply controls at the boundary where they are enforceable and observable. Use least privilege for identities, encryption for sensitive communication, explicit network paths, controlled deployment permissions and tested recovery procedures. Security and resilience must be verified continuously rather than assumed from the initial deployment.",
        "failureModes": [
          "Excessive permissions expose resources beyond the intended boundary.",
          "A single dependency or availability zone becomes an unrecognized single point of failure.",
