        "question": "What problem does Microservices solve?",
        "answer": "Microservices split a system into independently deployable services aligned to business capabilities. Their architecture requires service contracts, data ownership, discovery, observability and failure isolation. It provides a defined way to organize the components and responsibilities involved. In a production environment, the design should be selected according to workload requirements, security boundaries, operational capability and measurable service objectives."
      },
