          "Preserve evidence before making disruptive changes.",
          "Track recurring incidents and convert findings into automated safeguards."
        ],
        "explanation": "Important failure patterns include: Distributed monoliths, cascading failures, data inconsistency, excessive network calls and operational complexity. Troubleshooting should start with the user-visible symptom and move through the architecture one boundary at a time. Check recent changes, component health, access decisions, routing, dependency status and telemetry. Validate the recovery with a real request or workload test, then document the root cause and preventive action.",
