        "answer": "A Multi-AZ design distributes application capacity and, where supported, data services across independent availability zones within a region. It improves resilience against localized infrastructure failure. It provides a defined way to organize the components and responsibilities involved. In a production environment, the design should be selected according to workload requirements, security boundaries, operational capability and measurable service objectives."
