    "interviewQuestions": [
      {
        "question": "What problem does Monitoring Architecture solve?",
        "answer": "Monitoring architecture collects and evaluates metrics from applications, infrastructure and dependencies. It connects instrumentation to storage, alert evaluation, dashboards and incident response. It provides a defined way to organize the components and responsibilities involved. In a production environment, the design should be selected according to workload requirements, security boundaries, operational capability and measurable service objectives."
      },
