      },
      {
        "question": "What are the most important production risks?",
        "answer": "The key risks include Missing telemetry, noisy alerts, high-cardinality costs, stale dashboards and monitoring-system blind spots. Reduce them through explicit boundaries, least-privilege access, capacity planning, health monitoring, tested recovery procedures and controlled configuration changes. Verify the controls with practical failure tests."
      },
      {
        "question": "How would you troubleshoot a failure in this architecture?",
        "answer": "Start from the reported symptom and identify the affected user or workload path. Trace Applications and Infrastructure -> Metrics Exporters -> Collection and Scraping -> Time-Series Storage -> Alert Evaluation -> Dashboards and On-Call. Check recent changes, component health, permissions, routing, dependency responses and telemetry. Change one variable at a time and confirm recovery with an end-to-end test."
      },
      {
        "question": "Give a practical implementation example.",
        "answer": "Design monitoring for an API using request rate, error rate, latency and saturation signals with actionable alerts. Implement the design in a non-production environment first, document its dependencies and security controls, test normal and failure paths, and promote it through a reviewed deployment process. Capture metrics and logs so the production team can operate it reliably."
      }
    ],
